  "body": "MAINLINE-050 complete: 2,027,245-point weather maps for R10/12/15/20/30, all sixteen optimism subsets, zero surfaces, design cases and night-water accounts.\n\nAt 100 m, across RH0–100% and sea-pressure anomaly ±30 hPa, coupled day-design upper ISA offsets are +5.8/+9.5/+12.2/+14.3/+15.8 K. Fixed hulls sized for the full pressure range reduce those to −6.5/−3.0/−0.3/+1.8/+3.3 K. The projected cold-interface limit is about −10.5 K there. Design-family and fixed-vehicle claims are kept explicit.\n\nNo sampled radius floats on the declared MIL 10% hot profile, even at all four endpoints. Humidity and low-pressure marginals retain their missing coincident-weather assumptions.\n\nTwelve-hour deposition is approximately .085–.090 kg/m² in the reference clear case, .0035–.0038 overcast, .236–.243 saturated-clear, and .081–.084 cold frost. Latent heating prevents reference-case frost. R10 loses about 82 kg on the saturated-clear night. Drainage, heating, low-emittance, cover and morning-wait costs are supplied.\n\nFifteen numerical checks pass; 32 upstream pins match. All results remain QUESTIONABLE/PROJECTION; thirteen new NFIs and inherited registers remain open. Qualified installed-hull SF stays null. The refused sweep and explicit retry authority are preserved. The brief names no successor; this seat stops.",
